---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SOCIAL } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Christopher Chalcraft: geophysics roots, data at Databricks, Nix, Elixir, local-first software.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Hi, I'm Christopher.</p>
    <p>
      I came to software sideways, through geophysics and data science, where
      most of the work is pulling a clean signal out of a noisy world. That
      instinct stuck. I've spent years working with data, mostly making it
      correct, automated, and boring in the best way, and now I work at
      Databricks, with all of the awesome products in that stack.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm happiest a few layers down the stack. I run Linux, I configure
      everything I touch (Nix and Neovim, always), and I think a build that
      only works on one machine is a bug. I'm drawn to functional programming,
      Elixir in particular, to open source, and lately to local-first
      software: apps that keep working offline and use sync engines to
      reconcile later, like a network that heals itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from the terminal I play duplicate bridge, which turns out to be
      distributed systems with cards: partial information, a strict protocol,
      and a partner you have to trust. I also ride motorcycles and shoot film,
      probably the two most analog things I could find. Maybe that's the point.
    </p>
    <p>
      Feather &amp; Wire is where I write it all down: the feather is the
      writing, the wire is what it's about.
    </p>
    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      Long-form articles live here. Shorter notes go to <a href="https://blyg.featherandwire.dev/">Fragments</a>,
      a <a href="https://blygger.org/">Blygger</a> blyg, and the articles are
      published as one too, at <a href="/blyg/blyg.json">/blyg/</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, styled
      after Xe Iaso's <a href="https://design.within.website/">xess</a>, and
      deployed on Cloudflare Pages. The source is on <a href="https://github.com/cchalc/site">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      {SOCIAL.map((s) => (
        <li><a href={s.href} rel="me noopener">{s.label}</a></li>
      ))}
      <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
